This README file contains information on the contents of the meta-stevensuslipayload2627 layer.

Please see the corresponding sections below for details.

Dependencies
============

  URI: https://git.openembedded.org/openembedded-core
  branch: wrynose

  URI: https://git.yoctoproject.org/meta-yocto
  layers: meta-poky
  branch: wrynose

  URI: https://github.com/agherzan/meta-raspberrypi
  branch: wrynose

Patches
=======

Please submit changes to the meta-stevensuslipayload2627 layer as GitHub pull requests against:

  https://github.com/Stevens-Rocketry/RocketryUSLIPayloadYocto20262027

Maintainer: George Oliynyk <goliynyk@stevens.edu>

Table of Contents
=================

  I. Adding the meta-stevensuslipayload2627 layer to your build
 II. Misc


I. Adding the meta-stevensuslipayload2627 layer to your build
=============================================================

From an initialized wrynose build directory with meta-raspberrypi already added, run:

  bitbake-layers add-layer meta-stevensuslipayload2627
  bitbake-config-build enable-fragment machine/payload-pi4b
  bitbake-config-build enable-fragment distro/rocketrypayload
  bitbake payload-os-image

II. Misc
========

Machine: conf/machine/payload-pi4b.conf

  Raspberry Pi 4B, 64-bit. Extends raspberrypi4-64 from meta-raspberrypi and keeps its
  overrides active. Enables the serial console on GPIO 14/15 and sets the hostname to
  payload-dev-4B.

Distro: conf/distro/rocketrypayload.conf

  Stevens Rocketry USLI Payload OS, version 0.1. Based on Poky with systemd as the init
  manager. Accepts the synaptics-killswitch license required by the Pi 4 Wi-Fi/Bluetooth
  firmware.

Image: recipes-core/images/payload-os-image.bb

  Installs packagegroup-core-boot, packagegroup-rpi-test, procps, coreutils and util-linux
  on a root filesystem of at least 1 GiB. Builds only for Raspberry Pi machines.

  This is currently a development image: root has an empty password and is logged in
  automatically on the serial console. Remove the EXTRA_IMAGE_FEATURES line before
  building for flight.
